# mantra_snapshot_wire.rish -- I2 snapshot export: hosted + device Comlink crossing - 20260713.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/m/mantra_snapshot_wire.rish
#
# TWO ROWS, ONE PROMISE (20260910). The hosted half moved to its own file,
# tools/m/mantra_snapshot_hosted.rish, which this witness runs as its first leg --
# one body, so the two stay in agreement by construction. This file keeps its name
# and its whole promise: hosted AND device, GREEN only when both answer.
#
# Why the split: the device leg spawns qemu-system-riscv64, so on a bench without
# the emulator every run of this witness refused at that leg, and REDS %646 seats
# what follows -- a rostable witness is one whose every leg runs wherever the fleet
# stands, so a welded witness stays off construction/standing-equipment.kyri and its
# hosted asserts go unheard. The hosted row now runs on every lap of every bench,
# and this row carries `capability qemu_riscv`, so a bench with the emulator runs it
# whole and a bench without it reads `skipped_capability mantra_snapshot_wire
# wants=qemu_riscv here=absent` -- named on every pass rather than silent.
#
# The happy zone and the thin edge as a file boundary:
# foundations/20260826-194850_the-happy-zone-and-the-thin-edge.md.

let hosted = run ["rishi/bin/rishi" "run" "tools/m/mantra_snapshot_hosted.rish"]
say hosted.out
assert hosted.ok else "snapshot hosted witness refused -- run it alone to read its own leg"

let device = run ["sh" "comlink/run_snapshot_export_wire_lab.sh"]
say device.out
assert device.ok else "snapshot device wire lab refused"
assert device.out contains "GREEN" else "snapshot device wire lab not GREEN"

say "GREEN: I2 snapshot export hosted + device Comlink crossing witness passed."
